{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Human Security Layer.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Human Security Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"human security layer human security layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Human Security Layer.md","fileName":"Human Security Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Human Security Layer","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 02:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Layered Cyber Defense and Secure Development]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Layered Cyber Defense and Secure Development","Social Engineering","Defense in Depth","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Human Security Layer.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Human Security Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"human security layer human security layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Human Security Layer.md","fileName":"Human Security Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Human Security Layer","heading":"Human Security Layer","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The human security layer addresses the decisions, habits, and social interactions through which people affect a system's security. Training, clear procedures, careful identity verification, and usable controls reduce the chance that a person becomes the easiest route around technical defenses.\n\nBecause attackers can exploit trust through [[Social Engineering]], this layer belongs inside [[Defense in Depth]] rather than outside the technical system. Security design must account for how people actually work.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Layered Cyber Defense and Secure Development","Social Engineering","Defense in Depth","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Human Security Layer.md::2","sourceKey":"6